      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): bound webhook JSON response reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/discord/src/send.webhook.ts:124` calls raw `response.json()` on the webhook POST response. Without a byte cap, a misbehaving or compromised webhook endpoint could return an arbitrarily large response, exhausting memory.\n\n**Zero competition — no open PR covers this file.**\n\n## Changes\n\n- `send.webhook.ts`: replace unbounded `response.json()` with `readResponseWithLimit` capped at 1 MiB\n- Preserve tolerant parse: empty/malformed success bodies fall back to `{}` (Discord can return `204 No Content` when `wait=false`)\n- Add `test/_proof_discord_webhook_bounded_json.mts`: real node:http server proof\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests\n\n```\n$ pnpm exec vitest run extensions/discord/src/send.webhook.proxy.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\n### Real HTTP server proof\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx test/_proof_discord_webhook_bounded_json.mts\nPASS  oversized response (2 MiB > 1 MiB cap): bounded read rejects :: type=Error\nPASS  oversized response: error message mentions webhook JSON cap :: msg=Discord webhook JSON response too large: 1113941 bytes (limit: 1048576 bytes)\nPASS  normal response: parsed correctly :: id=msg-42, channel_id=C42\nPASS  empty body: falls back to {} without throwing :: payload={}\n\n[proof] 4 PASS, 0 FAIL\n```\n\n### Cap rationale\n\nDiscord webhook responses are < 1 KB. The 1 MiB cap is 1000x normal size and matches the standard bounded-read constant.\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted",
